Gates: SDD

Purpose:
  Automated Quality, Security & Release Gate Engine. Defines
  universal lifecycle and adaptive gates that determine when a
  task or release is ready. Task completion ≠ Release readiness.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1  @policy.sdd
   2  @levels.sdd
   3  @quality.sdd
   4  @testing.sdd
   5  @security.sdd
   6  @performance.sdd
   7  @infrastructure.sdd
   8  @release.sdd
   9  @exceptions.sdd
   10 @evidence.sdd

Modes:
  L0 — Prototype (minimal checks)
  L1 — Small project (basic test + lint)
  L2 — Production application (security + integration + deployment)
  L3 — Business-critical (performance + security + observability)
  L4 — High-scale (resilience + DR + advanced security)
  L5 — Mission-critical (formal controls + continuous verification)

Rules:
  [GT1]  Task completion ≠ Release readiness.
  [GT2]  Gates are adaptive: project context determines required gates.
  [GT3]  Every gate MUST have Condition + Evidence + Threshold + Owner + Decision.
  [GT4]  Gate failure blocks subsequent gates in chain.
  [GT5]  SKIPPED ≠ WAIVED: SKIPPED = not applicable, WAIVED = approved exception.
  [GT6]  Critical gates are hard blockers.
  [GT7]  Evidence MUST be stored for every gate result.
  [GT8]  Gate audit MUST record Who, What, When, Why, Result, Evidence.
  [GT9]  Waivers MUST have Reason, Owner, Expiration, Risk, Approval.
  [GT10] Expired waivers MUST re-trigger gate.
  [GT11] Incident feedback MUST trigger new gate requirements.
  [GT12] Gate chain: BDD → Code → Static Quality → Unit → Integration → E2E → Security → Performance → Infrastructure → Review → Release → Deploy → Runtime Verify.

Entry:
  Read:
    INDEX.sdd

  Resolve:
    policy
    levels
    quality
    testing
    security
    performance
    infrastructure
    release
    exceptions
    evidence

Navigation:
  Gates: @gates/INDEX.sdd
  Policy: @gates/policy.sdd
  Levels: @gates/levels.sdd
  Quality: @gates/quality.sdd
  Testing: @gates/testing.sdd
  Security: @gates/security.sdd
  Performance: @gates/performance.sdd
  Infrastructure: @gates/infrastructure.sdd
  Release: @gates/release.sdd
  Exceptions: @gates/exceptions.sdd
  Evidence: @gates/evidence.sdd
  ProjectGates: @project/gates/INDEX.sdd

State: +
  